      "sourceHash": "33719dd0c4c8f19631501e41a43a367182251d100f1f82e53784c89c78e79987",
      "contextFingerprint": "02eb224d2d41284635fdcc5b5e1c99682669770da438be9af3809c68bfd38810",
      "sourceText": "1.  相对延时\n\n    1.  函数：以下这俩函数作用相同，osDelay()和vTaskDelay()\n\n    2.  时间：是从调用该函数才开始算，直到延时指定时间结束\n\n    3.  调用方法：与HAL_Delay()方法一样\n\n    ```cpp\n    extern \"C\" //若在C++中运行需要加上该行\n    void green_led_task(void const * argument)\n    { \n        for(;;) //等同于while(true) \n        { \n        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_RESET); \n        osDelay(500); \n        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_SET); \n        osDelay(500); \n        }\n    }\n    ```\n\n2.  绝对延时\n\n    1.  函数：\n\n        1.  获取当前时间：osKernelSysTick()\n\n        2.  绝对延时函数：osDelayUntil()\n\n    2.  时间：从任务开始就开始算时间了，将整个任务运行周期看成一个整体，适用于按照一定频率运行的任务\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image250.webp)\n\n    4.  调用方法：\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image251.webp)\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image252.webp)",
      "translatedText": "1.  Relative delay\n\n    1.  Functions: The following two functions have the same effect, osDelay() and vTaskDelay()\n\n    2.  Timing: It starts counting only from when the function is called until the specified delay time ends\n\n    3.  Call method: Same as the HAL_Delay() method\n\n    ```cpp\n    extern \"C\" //若在C++中运行需要加上该行\n    void green_led_task(void const * argument)\n    { \n        for(;;) //等同于while(true) \n        { \n        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_RESET); \n        osDelay(500); \n        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_SET); \n        osDelay(500); \n        }\n    }\n    ```\n\n2.  Absolute delay\n\n    1.  Functions:\n\n        1.  Get current time: osKernelSysTick()\n\n        2.  Absolute delay function: osDelayUntil()\n\n    2.  Timing: Time starts counting from the beginning of the task; the entire task execution cycle is treated as a whole, suitable for tasks that run at a certain frequency\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image250.webp)\n\n    4.  Call method:\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image251.webp)\n\n    ![](https://cdn.tungchiahui.cn/tungwebsite/assets/images/2023/10/09/image252.webp)",
